{
  "title": "Eosinophil\u2013neutrophil co-elevation does not improve frozen prediction of expiratory airflow ratio across NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "A prespecified centered log-count interaction did not improve FEV1/FVC prediction over flexible marginal eosinophil and neutrophil counts and standard covariates: 2009\u201310 NHANES n=3996, paired weighted MSE gain -0.048557 percentage-points squared, target-PSU 95% interval -0.134868 to 0.023964. Source cross-validation also failed to improve. This negative test does not exclude inflammatory associations or other interactions, and is not a diagnostic study.",
